<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Healroot (RimWorld: Plant_Healroot)  - the plant herbal medicine comes from. Its own file, additively, for the
    reason CLAUDE.md gives.

    WHY IT EXISTS. MedicineHerbal had no source: a founding band started with some (Scenarios.xml) and once it was
    spent nothing on a map could make more, so the medicine lever ran dry and a settlement tended without it.
    Items_Medicine.xml recorded that as a gap. This closes it.

    THE NUMBERS are RimWorld's, from the wiki's healroot page (rimworldwiki.com/wiki/Healroot, infobox):
      growDays 7           "Time to grow 7 days (12.92 days with rest time)". Plant.TickLong's light curve gives
                           this port the same rest time (no growth between ~20:00 and ~07:00), so 7 here comes out
                           at roughly the wiki's 12.92 in practice  - it is not doubled to compensate.
      harvestYield 1       "Base harvest yield 1 herbal medicine". One medicine per plant, per cycle: this is a
                           slow source on purpose, which is why FarmingInitiative sizes a herb garden from it.
      MaxHitPoints 60      "HP 60".
      Flammability 1       "Flammability 1" (100%).
      sowMinSkill 8        "Minimum skill 8 (Plants)". The reason this port gained PlantProperties.sowMinSkill and
                           the check in WorkGiver_GrowerSow, ported from RimWorld's own.
      sowMinFertility 0.7  "Minimum fertility 70%". The wiki's version history says Beta 19/1.0 raised this from 50%
                           to 100% and grow time from 6.5 to 12 days, which contradicts the infobox the same page
                           carries for the current game (70% and 7 days). The two cannot both be right and the
                           decompile carries no Defs XML to settle it, so this takes the infobox, and NO test pins
                           these literals: the tests pin the behaviour (it needs good ground; it needs skill; it
                           harvests medicine), per CLAUDE.md. Fertility sensitivity "100%" is exactly this port's
                           growth model (Plant.TickLong multiplies by terrain fertility directly), so it needs no
                           field.
      pathCost 14          "Path cost 14".

    NOT PORTED, because PlantProperties (and the port around it) has no field for them: sow work 800 ticks and
    harvest work 400 ticks (JobDriver_Sow.SowWorkAmount / JobDriver_Harvest are shared, as the poplar's comment in
    Plants_Trees.xml already records for cutting), minimum light to grow 51%, the 0..58 C growth band (the port's
    PlantUtility curve is one curve for every plant), sow tags "Ground, Hydroponic" (a Zone_Growing names its plant
    directly), beauty, and the 0.2 nutrition animals graze it for (the port's plants are not ingestible; see the
    note in Plants_Food.xml). interferesWithRoof is left at its default false: RimWorld's healroot is not a tree
    and a roof may go up over it (it is the trees, via TreeBase, that set it).

    WHAT PICKS IT. FarmingInitiative.CropFor chooses the food crop and cannot choose this: MedicineHerbal has no
    nutrition, so its "nutrition per cell per day" is zero. FarmingInitiative.MedicineCropFor chooses it, for the
    separate herb garden a settlement paints when it is short of medicine.
  -->

  <ThingDef>
    <defName>Plant_Healroot</defName>
    <label>healroot</label>
    <description>A bitter-rooted herb that grows in good soil. Ground and dried, it makes herbal medicine. It takes a practised hand to sow.</description>
    <category>Plant</category>
    <thingClass>SimWorld.Building.Plant</thingClass>
    <tickerType>Long</tickerType>
    <passability>Standable</passability>
    <pathCost>14</pathCost>
    <useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
    <destroyable>true</destroyable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>1</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <growDays>7</growDays>
      <harvestedThingDef>MedicineHerbal</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>1</harvestYield>
      <sowMinFertility>0.7</sowMinFertility>
      <sowMinSkill>8</sowMinSkill>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
